{#import "./example/model.jx" as ExModel #}
{#import "./example/controller.jx" as ExController #}
{#import "./example/form.jx" as ExForm #}
{#import "./example/view.jx" as ExView #}

<section class="section example">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="example-block">
      <ExModel />
      <h3>Peewee ORM make modelling easy.</h3>
      <p>
        Proper uses Peewee as its ORM, and adds some extra features like
        scopes, rich text fields, and attachment support.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="example-block">
      <ExController />
      <h3>Controllers handle all requests.</h3>
      <p>
        Proper controllers are simple classes with methods for each action.
        They have before/after hooks, and can render templates or redirect.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="example-block">
      <ExForm class="example-short" />
      <h3>Forms are declarative and easy to use.</h3>
      <p>
        Proper forms are declarative, and integrate with Peewee models. They
        also have built-in validation, and can be rendered in templates.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="example-block">
      <ExView class="example-short" />
      <h3>Component Views.</h3>
      <p>
        Proper views are components-based templates. They
        can have props, slots, and can be nested.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>